Several correctness and hygiene issues across the core files: uninitialized struct returned to callers, missing return path (UB), `NULL` used on non-pointer types, and duplicate includes/double semicolons.

## Changes

### `OffSets.h`
- All 90+ offset variables marked `const` — none are ever written after definition

### `dllmain.cpp`
- `ReadInterface`: zero-initialize `RECT rectangle = {}` so callers don't receive garbage when the interface lookup fails
- `ReadUpTxt`: fix indentation
- Remove 4 accidental `;;` double-semicolons

### `MemoryError.h`
- Remove duplicate `#include <string>`

### `MemoryError.cpp`
- `DeterMemoryBlockLenght`: add missing `return {0, 0}` — all code paths previously reaching the end of the function without returning was UB
- `MyLocYRaw / MyLocXRaw / MyLocZRaw`: `NULL` → `0.0f` (non-pointer `FLOAT`)
- `PlaceHolderX / PlaceHolderY`: `NULL` → `0` (non-pointer `DWORD`)
- `CRL(FLOAT)` / `RXY(INT)`: `!= NULL` → `!= 0.0f` / `!= 0`

```cpp
// Before — UB: no return when blokk == NULL or Query fails
MEMss DeterMemoryBlockLenght(DWORD64 blokk) {
    MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION64 buffs = { 0 };
    if (blokk != NULL) {
        if (proc.remote().memory().Query(blokk, &buffs) == STATUS_SUCCESS)
            return { buffs.AllocationBase, buffs.RegionSize };
    }
} // ← falls off the end

// After
    return { 0, 0 };
}
```

